{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YT9fkbK578HjSu8pdnd2ZR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-281 — smoke tier true to its name: ≤ 60 s commit bar + a declared runtime budget\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-281 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** the meta commit bar\n4\t(tests/conftest.py WI-122 tiering + the declared bar in status.md); no spine SR\n5\t— test-harness layer, 150-row empty-`SR-Refs` precedent.\n6\t\n7\t## Problem\n8\t\n9\tThe smoke tier is not a smoke test. Tiering is **opt-OUT** (WI-122,\n10\t`tests/conftest.py::SLOW_MODULES`): every collected test is `smoke` unless its\n11\tmodule is one of 15 named heavy end-to-end modules — so the commit bar runs\n12\t**1088 of 1378 tests (79%)**. Measured on the dev box (2026-07-23, 3.11.9 venv,\n13\t`-n auto`, three runs): **6:12 / 6:51 / 8:01 wall** — against a declared\n14\t\"~3.3 min\" in status.md that was already generous. The owner's directive\n15\t(2026-07-23): a smoke test answers *\"is it basically alive?\"* — the per-commit\n16\tbar should run in **≤ 60 seconds**, and the runtime should be **its own\n17\tdeclared budget item** so drift is caught, not re-discovered.\n18\t\n19\tWhy it matters: the bar's cost shapes behavior. Sessions pay it on every\n20\tcommit (the session-protocol §3 commit bar), so a 7-minute \"smoke\" either slows\n21\tevery loop iteration or tempts skipping the bar — both worse than a fast bar\n22\tplus the unchanged full suite at slice/phase close and in CI.\n23\t\n24\tThe WI-122 intent worth preserving: opt-out means a NEW test lands in the\n25\tcommit bar by default (\"never a false green\" by omission), and `smoke`/`slow`\n26\t**partition** the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` guards it). The intent worth\n27\tcorrecting: at 1378 tests the generous default has inverted the tier's\n28\tpurpose.\n29\t\n30\t## Approach\n31\t\n32\tTwo deliverables — the re-tier and the budget sensor. Measure first, then cut:\n33\t\n34\t- **(a) Measure.** One `-m smoke --durations=0` run (plus per-module wall\n35\t  totals); record the module-level ranking in the close deliverable. Expected\n36\t  shape: the cost concentrates in modules driving subprocesses / bootstrapped\n37\t  scaffolds through `conftest.run_py` (subprocess-coverage overhead included) —\n38\t  the same class the existing 15 SLOW_MODULES already name.\n39\t- **(b) Re-tier to the budget.** Preferred: **keep the opt-out partition**\n40\t  (new tests still default into the bar) but move whole modules to `slow` by\n41\t  the measured ranking until smoke fits ≤ 60 s with headroom (~45 s target),\n42\t  drawing the line at the mechanical boundary where possible (subprocess/\n43\t  scaffold modules out; in-process unit modules in). Fallback if the budget\n44\t  cannot hold that way: flip to the **opt-IN `@smoke` posture the kit itself\n45\t  ships** (`project-trajectory/pytest.ini` uses opt-in marks with unmarked =\n46\t  full-suite-only — the meta-repo would then match its own template; note the\n47\t  erosion risk: new tests default OUT of the bar). Record whichever line is\n48\t  drawn and why in the spec/close notes.\n49\t- **(c) The budget item.** Declare the budget once and give it a sensor that\n50\t  bites, in the repo's growth-sensor idiom (`test_module_size_ratchet.py`,\n51\t  `test_dashboard_size_budget.py`):\n52\t  - **Declared home:** a `smoke-budget` entry alongside the tier declaration\n53\t    (docs/stack.ini `[tiers]` vicinity) — seconds for humans/CI, plus the\n54\t    deterministic proxy below.\n55\t  - **Deterministic sensor (always-on):** wall-clock asserts are\n56\t    machine-dependent and flaky, so the *ratchet* budgets what is\n57\t    deterministic — smoke-tier **membership** (collected-count ceiling, and/or\n58\t    the SLOW_MODULES line itself). Exceeding it fails the suite with the\n59\t    \"raise deliberately or re-tier\" message the size ratchets use.\n60\t  - **Wall-clock check (where timing is stable):** CI times the smoke step\n61\t    against the declared seconds budget (warn locally, enforce in CI — the\n62\t    build session picks warn-vs-fail per lane and records it).\n63\t- **(d) Update the declared surfaces** that state the bar's cost/shape:\n64\t  status.md \"Bar (per commit)\" (~3.3 min text), the `pytest.ini` header\n65\t  comment, `tests/conftest.py`'s WI-122 block, and the `session-protocol`\n66\t  skill §3 if it names the runtime. `test_smoke_tier.py`'s partition guard\n67\t  stays green throughout.\n68\t\n69\t**Hard edges:** no test is deleted or weakened — re-tiered only; the full\n70\tsuite (`-q -n auto`, slice/phase close + CI) is untouched; `smoke`+`slow`\n71\tremain a total partition.\n72\t\n73\t## Interfaces\n74\t\n75\tNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/` (conftest tiering, the new\n76\tbudget sensor, `test_smoke_tier.py`), `pytest.ini`, and the declared-bar prose\n77\thomes (docs/status.md, docs/stack.ini comment vicinity, the session-protocol\n78\tskill). Intra-module, test/harness layer. Nearest seam for reference: SR-007's\n79\tdeclared stack profile (`docs/stack.ini [tiers]` is already the tier\n80\tdeclaration check.py reads), unchanged in shape.\n81\t\n82\t## Done-when\n83\t\n84\t- [ ] Measured module ranking recorded; the re-tiered smoke runs **≤ 60 s**\n85\t      wall at `-n auto` on the dev box (real output pasted; ~45 s target for\n86\t      headroom).\n87\t- [ ] `smoke`/`slow` still partition the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` green);\n88\t      no test deleted; full suite count unchanged.\n89\t- [ ] The budget item exists: declared value + deterministic membership\n90\t      ratchet that **bites** (mutating the tier past the ceiling fails), and\n91\t      the CI wall-clock check wired with its warn/fail choice recorded.\n92\t- [ ] Declared surfaces updated (status.md bar text, pytest.ini header,\n93\t      conftest WI-122 block, session-protocol §3 if it names the runtime).\n94\t- [ ] Commit bar green — run with the NEW tier (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke`\n95\t      + `check_docs.py`) plus one full-suite run proving nothing was lost.\n96\t- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n97\t      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n98\t\n99\t## Notes / open questions\n100\t\n101\t- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive: \"a smoke test is supposed to be just\n102\t  that\"). **Re-fronted the same day (owner ruling): `Priority=1`** — the id\n103\t  tie-break keeps WI-275 first, this WI second, so every subsequent session's\n104\t  commit bar runs against the tightened tier.\n105\t- The 79% smoke share means the bar currently *re-runs most of the full suite*\n106\t  per commit — the cut is large by construction; expect smoke to land in the\n107\t  low hundreds of tests. Anything cut still runs at slice/phase close + CI.\n108\t- If the dev box's `-n auto` worker count materially differs from CI's, the\n109\t  seconds budget is per-lane; the deterministic membership ratchet is the\n110\t  shared floor — this is why the budget item is split in two.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7389bb9f-9f9a-499d-87c4-4c422632b100","uuid":"997afcf0-1af5-4aab-851e-44b9fc32b977","timestamp":"2026-07-23T07:41:58.984Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9\\docs\\specs\\WI-281.md","content":"# WI-281 — smoke tier true to its name: ≤ 60 s commit bar + a declared runtime budget\n\n**WI:** WI-281 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** the meta commit bar\n(tests/conftest.py WI-122 tiering + the declared bar in status.md); no spine SR\n— test-harness layer, 150-row empty-`SR-Refs` precedent.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe smoke tier is not a smoke test. Tiering is **opt-OUT** (WI-122,\n`tests/conftest.py::SLOW_MODULES`): every collected test is `smoke` unless its\nmodule is one of 15 named heavy end-to-end modules — so the commit bar runs\n**1088 of 1378 tests (79%)**. Measured on the dev box (2026-07-23, 3.11.9 venv,\n`-n auto`, three runs): **6:12 / 6:51 / 8:01 wall** — against a declared\n\"~3.3 min\" in status.md that was already generous. The owner's directive\n(2026-07-23): a smoke test answers *\"is it basically alive?\"* — the per-commit\nbar should run in **≤ 60 seconds**, and the runtime should be **its own\ndeclared budget item** so drift is caught, not re-discovered.\n\nWhy it matters: the bar's cost shapes behavior. Sessions pay it on every\ncommit (the session-protocol §3 commit bar), so a 7-minute \"smoke\" either slows\nevery loop iteration or tempts skipping the bar — both worse than a fast bar\nplus the unchanged full suite at slice/phase close and in CI.\n\nThe WI-122 intent worth preserving: opt-out means a NEW test lands in the\ncommit bar by default (\"never a false green\" by omission), and `smoke`/`slow`\n**partition** the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` guards it). The intent worth\ncorrecting: at 1378 tests the generous default has inverted the tier's\npurpose.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo deliverables — the re-tier and the budget sensor. Measure first, then cut:\n\n- **(a) Measure.** One `-m smoke --durations=0` run (plus per-module wall\n  totals); record the module-level ranking in the close deliverable. Expected\n  shape: the cost concentrates in modules driving subprocesses / bootstrapped\n  scaffolds through `conftest.run_py` (subprocess-coverage overhead included) —\n  the same class the existing 15 SLOW_MODULES already name.\n- **(b) Re-tier to the budget.** Preferred: **keep the opt-out partition**\n  (new tests still default into the bar) but move whole modules to `slow` by\n  the measured ranking until smoke fits ≤ 60 s with headroom (~45 s target),\n  drawing the line at the mechanical boundary where possible (subprocess/\n  scaffold modules out; in-process unit modules in). Fallback if the budget\n  cannot hold that way: flip to the **opt-IN `@smoke` posture the kit itself\n  ships** (`project-trajectory/pytest.ini` uses opt-in marks with unmarked =\n  full-suite-only — the meta-repo would then match its own template; note the\n  erosion risk: new tests default OUT of the bar). Record whichever line is\n  drawn and why in the spec/close notes.\n- **(c) The budget item.** Declare the budget once and give it a sensor that\n  bites, in the repo's growth-sensor idiom (`test_module_size_ratchet.py`,\n  `test_dashboard_size_budget.py`):\n  - **Declared home:** a `smoke-budget` entry alongside the tier declaration\n    (docs/stack.ini `[tiers]` vicinity) — seconds for humans/CI, plus the\n    deterministic proxy below.\n  - **Deterministic sensor (always-on):** wall-clock asserts are\n    machine-dependent and flaky, so the *ratchet* budgets what is\n    deterministic — smoke-tier **membership** (collected-count ceiling, and/or\n    the SLOW_MODULES line itself). Exceeding it fails the suite with the\n    \"raise deliberately or re-tier\" message the size ratchets use.\n  - **Wall-clock check (where timing is stable):** CI times the smoke step\n    against the declared seconds budget (warn locally, enforce in CI — the\n    build session picks warn-vs-fail per lane and records it).\n- **(d) Update the declared surfaces** that state the bar's cost/shape:\n  status.md \"Bar (per commit)\" (~3.3 min text), the `pytest.ini` header\n  comment, `tests/conftest.py`'s WI-122 block, and the `session-protocol`\n  skill §3 if it names the runtime. `test_smoke_tier.py`'s partition guard\n  stays green throughout.\n\n**Hard edges:** no test is deleted or weakened — re-tiered only; the full\nsuite (`-q -n auto`, slice/phase close + CI) is untouched; `smoke`+`slow`\nremain a total partition.\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/` (conftest tiering, the new\nbudget sensor, `test_smoke_tier.py`), `pytest.ini`, and the declared-bar prose\nhomes (docs/status.md, docs/stack.ini comment vicinity, the session-protocol\nskill). Intra-module, test/harness layer. Nearest seam for reference: SR-007's\ndeclared stack profile (`docs/stack.ini [tiers]` is already the tier\ndeclaration check.py reads), unchanged in shape.\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [ ] Measured module ranking recorded; the re-tiered smoke runs **≤ 60 s**\n      wall at `-n auto` on the dev box (real output pasted; ~45 s target for\n      headroom).\n- [ ] `smoke`/`slow` still partition the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` green);\n      no test deleted; full suite count unchanged.\n- [ ] The budget item exists: declared value + deterministic membership\n      ratchet that **bites** (mutating the tier past the ceiling fails), and\n      the CI wall-clock check wired with its warn/fail choice recorded.\n- [ ] Declared surfaces updated (status.md bar text, pytest.ini header,\n      conftest WI-122 block, session-protocol §3 if it names the runtime).\n- [ ] Commit bar green — run with the NEW tier (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke`\n      + `check_docs.py`) plus one full-suite run proving nothing was lost.\n- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive: \"a smoke test is supposed to be just\n  that\"). **Re-fronted the same day (owner ruling): `Priority=1`** — the id\n  tie-break keeps WI-275 first, this WI second, so every subsequent session's\n  commit bar runs against the tightened tier.\n- The 79% smoke share means the bar currently *re-runs most of the full suite*\n  per commit — the cut is large by construction; expect smoke to land in the\n  low hundreds of tests. Anything cut still runs at slice/phase close + CI.\n- If the dev box's `-n auto` worker count materially differs from CI's, the\n  seconds budget is per-lane; the deterministic membership ratchet is the\n  shared floor — this is why the budget item is split in two.\n","numLines":111,"startLine":1,"totalLines":111}}}
